Oops the second edit produced:
```js
net.on('levelup', () => {
  this.ui.refresh();
});
```
`ui.refresh()` renders panel if open; fine but weird. Actually it's harmless. But better no handler at all? Keep.

Now startNew: set levelCheck after state. It's initialized 1; xp 0 → level 1. fine.

Now server fixes: npcHit broadcast, respawn, remove levelup? Keep levelup. Also `cannonDamage` import used. `xpForLevel` used.

Server fire handler:
```js
const res = sim.damageNpc(...);
if (res.ok) broadcast({t:'event', ...sim.events.find(e=>e.type==='npcHit')});
```
Replace with broadcast explicit using npc coords. Ability similarly pushes events not broadcast; add broadcast per damage? Instead broadcast ability event; clients see ring. Damage visuals optional. But hp sync via snapshot.

Also server must broadcast sink/loot events from damageNpc (pushed to sim.events, which will be cleared on next tick before broadcasting). Since damageNpc happens between ticks, those sink/loot events may be lost! The tick clears events at start. So sink caused by player fire might never broadcast. Need to handle: after damageNpc, if res.sank, broadcast sink event + lootSpawn. Sim's events hold them; grab immediately. Implement helper `flushCombatEvents()` that scans sim.events for npcHit/sink/lootSpawn and broadcasts + clears? But tick events later broadcast anyway; duplicates possible if same event remains until tick. Since tick clears events at start, flush immediately then clear sim.events to avoid double. But careful: tick events (NPC shots) are broadcast in setInterval; if we clear mid-tick not an issue (single-threaded).

Implement in fire handler:
```js
const res = sim.damageNpc(...);
if (res.ok) {
  for (const ev of sim.events) {
    if (ev.type==='npcHit'||ev.type==='sink'||ev.type==='lootSpawn') broadcast({t:'event',...ev});
  }
  sim.events.length = 0;
}
```
Same for ability.

But then `lootSpawn` event broadcast — client onServerEvent doesn't handle lootSpawn (sync via snapshot). Fine.

Also NPC firing events in tick: tick returns events, server broadcasts shot/sink/spawn; playerHit handled. Good. Note tick events include npcHit? no.

Respawn: in tick events, type respawn has playerId, x,z. In setInterval add:
```js
if (ev.type==='respawn') { const target = sockets.get(ev.playerId); if (target) send(target, {t:'event', type:'respawn', x:ev.x, z:ev.z}); }
```
Client onServerEvent handles respawn (I added). Good.

Also `sim.tick` sets p.alive false and then respawns after 6s. Client handles death at 5s. Server's respawn event at 6s sets pos again to (0,60) while client at (0,140). Minor; make server respawn at (0,140)? Change sim respawn position to x=0,z=140 and player start 60. Actually sim uses p.x=0,p.z=60. Let's set 140 to match. And client onServerEvent respawn sets pos to ev.x/ev.z (140). Fine.

Also server `join` player pos from client; if client at 120.

Patch server.

Also remove unused import `xpForLevel`? used in levelup. Fine.

Now UI `panelShipyard` fix done.

Next: package.json scripts + start. Check package.json.

