content.text:
I accidentally wrote `.editor { width: min(560px, 100%); }` in the edit but my newString says `.editor { width: min(560px, 100%); }`? The output shows `.editor { width: min(560px, 100%); }` — hmm I typed `min(560px, 100%)` and it shows `min(560px, 100%)`. Fine.

Wait the oldString had `width: min(560px, 100%)`? original was `.editor { width: min(560px, 100%); }` — yes.

Now add compact height rule. Also adjust breakpoint usage for `#start-screen` mobile.

Add at end:
```css
@media (max-height: 780px) and (min-width: 941px) {
  .feature-row { display:none; }
  .tagline { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .brand h1 { font-size: 58px; }
}
```

Also at 1024x768 the editor may still exceed: compute: editor padding 20+16=36; head 40; field 65; 3 blocks: faction 7+58 + head 20 = 85; fruit 85; ship 85; button 45; links 30; fineprint 20 → total ~ 36+40+65+255+45+30+20 = 491. Good. Brand: kicker 20 + title 2*? 84px*0.92*2 lines ≈ 155 + tagline 50 + features 30 ≈ 255. Fits 768.

Let's reload screenshot.

